message.content:
I see! The `DitherContext` struct has a `LastRandomNumber` array that is NOT initialized in `FLAC__replaygain_synthesis__init_dither_context`. The `init_dither_context` function initializes `ErrorHistory`, `DitherHistory`, `FilterCoeff`, `Mask`, `Add`, `Dither`, and `LastHistoryIndex`, but NOT `LastRandomNumber`.

In `dither_output_`, when `shapingtype == 0` (NOISE_SHAPING_NONE), it reads `d->LastRandomNumber[k]`:
```c
if(shapingtype == 0) {
    double  tmp = random_equi_(d->Dither);
    Sum2 = tmp - d->LastRandomNumber [k];  // <-- reads uninitialized value!
    d->LastRandomNumber [k] = (int)tmp;
    ...
}
```

This is the "Use-of-uninitialized-value" bug! When `noise_shaping` is set to `NOISE_SHAPING_NONE` (0), the `dither_output_` function reads `d->LastRandomNumber[k]` which is never initialized.

Now, let me check if this was fixed in a later commit. Let me look at the git history for this file.

